From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: retain 2048 MAC buffers for Sheng firmware

The WCN7850 on Xiaomi Sheng uses WLAN.HMT.1.1.c2-00259 firmware. With
4096 MAC buffers, firmware initialization completes but the first MAC
start exhausts the two HTC credits and WMI_PDEV_SET_PARAM times out.
Restoring 2048 buffers permits interface startup and credit replenishment.
The larger RX release ring can be retained.

Upstream commit 58aeb412495a increased the MAC buffer count to 4096 for
throughput stability, tested with newer HMT.1.1.c5-00302 firmware. Keep
that default for other boards and limit this compatibility workaround to
Sheng's WCN7850. This is a local workaround, not an upstream patch.

Related-upstream: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=58aeb412495ada7fe5495c7805504d7cf1d45453
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <linux/fips.h>
 #include <linux/ieee80211.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/skbuff.h>
 #include "core.h"
 #include "debug.h"
@@ -1693,6 +1694,7 @@
 int ath12k_dp_rx_alloc(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_dp *dp = ath12k_ab_to_dp(ab);
+	u32 mac_buf_ring_size = DP_RX_MAC_BUF_RING_SIZE;
 	struct dp_srng *srng;
 	int i, ret;
 
@@ -1708,12 +1710,17 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/* Sheng's HMT.1.1.c2 firmware stalls WMI with 4096 MAC buffers. */
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20 &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,sheng"))
+		mac_buf_ring_size = 2048;
+
 	if (ab->hw_params->rx_mac_buf_ring) {
 		for (i = 0; i < ab->hw_params->num_rxdma_per_pdev; i++) {
 			ret = ath12k_dp_srng_setup(ab,
 						   &dp->rx_mac_buf_ring[i],
 						   HAL_RXDMA_BUF, 1,
-						   i, DP_RX_MAC_BUF_RING_SIZE);
+						   i, mac_buf_ring_size);
 			if (ret) {
 				ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to setup rx_mac_buf_ring %d\n",
 					    i);
